🎵 Sonia for Android — Quick start (English)
===========================================

Tap an icon on your home screen, and your music is ready.

STEP 1 — Install the apps (one time)
  From F-Droid (https://f-droid.org/packages/com.termux/), install:
    - Termux          (required)
    - Termux:Widget   (recommended: home-screen shortcut)
  Tip: install ALL Termux apps from F-Droid. Do not mix them with Google Play versions.

STEP 2 — Install Sonia (copy, paste, Enter in Termux)

  curl -sL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yasuhito3/Sonia-for-Android/main/install.sh | bash

  Allow storage access when Android asks. Sonia opens automatically when it's done.

STEP 3 — Put the icon on your home screen
  In Chrome (where Sonia just opened):
    Menu (⋮) -> "Install app"  (or "Add to Home screen")
  You can also do it from Sonia's SET tab -> "Add to Home screen".

DAILY USE
  Sonia runs inside Termux's screen; the browser is just its remote panel.
  1. Tap the "Sonia" Termux:Widget shortcut (or type `musica` in Termux).
     The browser opens by itself in a few seconds.
  2. Pick a song (MUSIC / RADIO / STREAM).
  3. Press Home — music keeps playing. Leave Termux alone; do NOT swipe it away
     from "recent apps" (that stops Sonia too).
  4. To quit: SET tab -> "Quit Sonia".

IF YOU SEE "Sonia is resting"
  Sonia isn't running. Tap the Termux:Widget "Sonia" shortcut
  (long-press home screen -> Widgets -> Termux:Widget -> choose "Sonia").
  The page reconnects automatically.

COMMANDS (in Termux)
  musica                    start and open in the browser
  musica stop               quit (from another Termux session)
  musica status             is it running?
  musica update             update to the latest version
  musica autostart on|off   experimental: start at boot (may be stopped by Android)
  musica log                show the log

TROUBLESHOOTING
  - No songs?          Run `termux-setup-storage`, put files in /sdcard/Music, then SET -> Rescan.
  - Music stops when the screen is off?
                       Android Settings -> Apps -> Termux -> Battery -> "Unrestricted".
  - No "Install app"?  Open http://localhost:8080 in Chrome (not via an IP address).
    "Add to Home screen" in the menu works too.

